    "q-110589": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110589",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find, in descending powers of $t,$ the first three terms of the binomial expansion of $(t+2)^{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's compare our expression with the binomial\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}.\n$$\n\nHere we have that $n=4,$ $a=t,$ and $b=2.$ So, the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{a}^{4}{b}^{0},\\,{a}^{3}{b}^{1},\\,{a}^{2}{b}^{2},\\,{a}^{1}{b}^{3},\\,{a}^{0}{b}^{4}.\n$$\n\nThe $4$th row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,4,6,4,1).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t+2)^{4} & =1{a}^{4}{b}^{0}+4{a}^{3}b+6{a}^{2}{b}^{2}+4a{b}^{3}+1{b}^{4} \\\\  & =1(t)^{4}(2)^{0}+4(t)^{3}(2)^{1}+6(t)^{2}(2)^{2}+4(t)^{1}(2)^{3}+1(t)^{0}(2)^{4} \\\\  & =1({t}^{4})(1)+4({t}^{3})(2)+6({t}^{2})({2}^{2})+4(t)({2}^{3})+1({t}^{0})({2}^{4}) \\\\  & ={t}^{4}+8{t}^{3}+24{t}^{2}+32t+16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in descending powers of $t,$ the first three terms of the binomial expansion are\n\n$$\n{t}^{4}+8{t}^{3}+24{t}^{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
