    "q-3744": {
      "dom_id": "step-q3744",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n{(r+m)}^{3}=A{r}^{3}+B{r}^{2}m+Cr{m}^{2}+{m}^{3}\n$$\n\nwhere $A,B$ and $C$ are constants, determine the value of $A+B+C.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's compare our expression with the binomial\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}.\n$$\n\nHere we have that $n=3,$ $a=r,$ and $b=m.$ So, the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}{b}^{0},\\,{a}^{2}{b}^{1},\\,{a}^{1}{b}^{2},\\,{a}^{0}{b}^{3}.\n$$\n\nThe $3$rd row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,3,3,1).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r+m)^{3} & =1{a}^{3}+3{a}^{2}b+3a{b}^{2}+1{b}^{3} \\\\  & =1(r)^{3}(m)^{0}+3(r)^{2}(m)^{1}+3(r)^{1}(m)^{2}+1(r)^{0}(m)^{3} \\\\  & =1({r}^{3})(1)+3({r}^{2})(m)+3(r)({m}^{2})+1(1)({m}^{3}) \\\\  & ={r}^{3}+3{r}^{2}m+3r{m}^{2}+{m}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=1,B=3,$ and $C=3.$ Finally, then\n\n$$\nA+B+C=1+3+3=7.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
