    "q-12875": {
      "dom_id": "step-q12875",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n{(y+{x}^{2})}^{3}={y}^{3}+A{y}^{2}{x}^{2}+By{x}^{4}+C{x}^{6}\n$$\n\nwhere $A,B$ and $C$ are constants, determine the value of $A+B+C.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's compare our expression with the binomial\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}.\n$$\n\nHere we have that $n=3,$ $a=y,$ and $b={x}^{2}.$ So, the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}{b}^{0},\\,{a}^{2}{b}^{1},\\,{a}^{1}{b}^{2},\\,{a}^{0}{b}^{3}.\n$$\n\nThe $3$rd row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,3,3,1).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(y+{x}^{2})}^{3} & =1{a}^{3}+3{a}^{2}b+3a{b}^{2}+1{b}^{3} \\\\  & =1(y)^{3}{({x}^{2})}^{0}+3(y)^{2}{({x}^{2})}^{1}+3(y)^{1}{({x}^{2})}^{2}+1(y)^{0}{({x}^{2})}^{3} \\\\  & =1{y}^{3}(1)+3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}+3y{x}^{4}+1(1){x}^{6} \\\\  & ={y}^{3}+3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}+3y{x}^{4}+{x}^{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=3,B=3,$ and $C=1.$ Finally, then\n\n$$\nA+B+C=3+3+1=7.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
