    "q-110705": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110705",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find the coefficient of ${t}^{9}$ in the expansion of  ${(4-2{t}^{3})}^{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the exponent of the binomial expression is $n=4,$ we see that the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{({t}^{3})}^{0},\\,{({t}^{3})}^{1},\\,{({t}^{3})}^{2},\\,{({t}^{3})}^{3},\\,{({t}^{3})}^{4}\n$$\n\nOf these, the term that returns ${t}^{9}$ is the fourth. So, we are looking for the fourth term in the binomial expansion.\n\nThe $4$th row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,4,6,4,1).$ Therefore, the fourth term in the binomial expansion is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({4}^{1}){(-2{t}^{3})}^{3} & =4(4)(-8{t}^{9})=-128{t}^{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coefficient of ${t}^{9}$ in the expansion of ${(4-2{t}^{3})}^{4}$ is $-128.$",
